{"id": "borderline-descriptive-imperative", "label": "benign-tricky", "expect": "PROMOTE", "agent": "teaching-prep", "slug": "parameterized-queries-prevent-sql-injection", "summary": "Always use parameterized queries instead of concatenating user input into SQL; this is the baseline defense against SQL injection", "excerpt": "Decisions:\n- Capture the parameterized-queries rule as a reusable teaching concept\nFindings:\n- Students who concatenate input ship injectable code; parameter binding fixes it\n- A durable secure-coding principle, not a one-off"}
